+2. **Verify every finding scored 50 or higher** by reading the cited line or re-running the
+   reviewer's stated command. Write a new probe only when a blocking finding has no reproduction
+   at all. A finding whose evidence does not hold goes to the dropped list with the fact that
+   disproved it.
+3. **False premises are findings.** Re-read the citation of every FALSE row in scope 1's premise
+   audit. Each false claim in a comment, a docstring, the commit message, or the PR body scores
+   50 or higher, with the fix "state the actual behavior and remove the wrong rationale". This
+   holds when the code behaves correctly despite the claim, and when you used the same fact to
+   settle a disagreement between the reviewers.
